<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine monthly oilseed crushings.</title>
<headline>Argentine monthly oilseed crushings.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine mills crushed 1,658,274 tonnes of oilseed in July 1996 against 1,432,274 tonnes in July 1995, the Agriculture Secretariat said. (Breakdown in tonnes, year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> Soybean	     1,110,497    (866,314)</p>
<p> Sunflowerseed	 434,484    (459,653)</p>
<p> Linseed		   6,855	(9,264)</p>
<p> Groundnutseed	  16,633     (19,733)</p>
<p> Cottonseed	     90,256     (77,318)</p>
<p>Output in July was as follows:</p>
<p> ..............Oils...................Meals</p>
<p> Soybean     187,581    (150,703)    855,895     (685,668)</p>
<p> Sunflower   175,952    (184,552)    179,370     (192,960)</p>
<p> Linseed	 2,117	(3,031)	  nil	   (nil)</p>
<p> Groundnut     6,515	(7,656)	9,302	(11,155)</p>
<p> Cottonseed   14,176     (11,633)     43,768	(29,869)</p>
<p> .......................Expellers</p>
<p> Soybean    2,320   (4,843)  Groundnut   nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Sunflower    nil     (333)  Cottonseed  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Linseed	nil     (nil)</p>
<p>Crushings from January to July, with the same period in 1995 in brackets, were:</p>
<p> Soybean	     5,234,431    (4,356,914)</p>
<p> Sunflowerseed     3,371,033    (3,110,642)</p>
<p> Linseed		  98,354	 (49,183)</p>
<p> Groundnutseed	  55,246	 (49,183)</p>
<p> Cottonseed	    327,452	(303,199)</p>
<p>Output in January through July (1995 in brackets):</p>
<p> ..............Oils...................Meals</p>
<p> Soybean     930,330    (742,644)  4,190,249  (3,412,247)</p>
<p> Sunflower 1,313,016  (1,242,160)  1,380,290  (1,340,944)</p>
<p> Linseed	32,475     (29,771)	  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Groundnut    23,679     (19,190)     35,844     (27,466)</p>
<p> Cottonseed   50,173     (46,403)    153,285    (137,624)</p>
<p> .......................Expellers</p>
<p> Soybean    22,000 (34,483)   Groundnut   nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Sunflower   5,588  (2,114)   Cottonseed  nil	  (nil)</p>
<p> Linseed    69,895 (59,844)</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541-318-0655</p>
